# de Longchamps point — the reflection of H over O is the orthocenter of the anticomplementary triangle (source: de Longchamps; Altshiller-Court, College Geometry)
A B C = triangle
O = circumcenter(A, B, C)
H = orthocenter(A, B, C)
L = reflect(H, O)
A2 = parallelogram(B, A, C)
B2 = parallelogram(A, B, C)
C2 = parallelogram(A, C, B)
prove perp(A2, L, B2, C2)
